denops/denops-helloworld.vim/blob/main/README.md#dependencies\u003e ここのdlinkってもう使ってないですよね？","ts":"1625817608.341500","attachments":[{"color":"24292f","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim-denops/denops-helloworld.vim/blob/main/README.md | README.md\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim-denops/denops-helloworld.vim/blob/main/README.md | README.md\u003e","text":"*denops-helloworld.vim*\n\nAn example plugin of \u003chttps://github.com/vim-denops/denops.vim|denops.vim\u003e.\n\nUse your favorite Vim plugin manager to install it.\n\n*Usage*\n\nUse one of the following commands to test the features:\n\nOr use `denops#request({name}, {fn}, {args})` to call a function and get the  \nresult like\n\n```\necho denops#request(\"helloworld\", \"say\", [\"World\"])\n\n```\n\nOr use `denops#notify({name}, {fn}, {params})` to call a function and leave like\n\n```\ncall denops#notify(\"helloworld\", \"say\", [\"World\"])\n\n```\n\nSome APIs of this sample plugin are not defined as commands so user need to use  \n`denops#request()` or `denops#notify()` to invoke it. See  \n\u0026lt;./denops/helloworld/main.ts|`main.ts`\u0026gt; to find out what's more.\n\nSee  \n\u003chttps://doc.deno.land/https/deno.land/x/denops_std/mod.ts|deno doc for denops_std\u003e  \nfor API details.\n\n*Dependencies*\n\nThis plugin use \u003chttps://github.com/keroxp/dlink|dlink\u003e to manage deno modules.","mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/vim-denops/denops-helloworld.vim|vim-denops/denops-helloworld.vim\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"8xr"}]},{"type":"message","user":"U023ANT1TME","text":"\u003c@U023ANT1TME\u003e has joined the channel","ts":"1625807023.339500","subtype":"channel_join","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":null},{"client_msg_id":"a28a3d04-ff7f-4c34-93d2-e1d1de5